      ":question/id": "9b628f87-c642-53b2-a35d-dc7358bbfdba",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {x}^{2}{6}^{{x}^{3}/5}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{5}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{6}^{{x}^{3}/5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {6}^{{x}^{3}/5}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {6}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\int {6}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot {6}^{u}}{3\\operatorname{ln}\u20616}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot {6}^{{x}^{3}/5}}{3\\operatorname{ln}\u20616}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
